think I was cool enough to be her friend. Rui En grabbed the bin. It was heavier than she expected, the rotting smell stinging her eyes, making her legs wobble. Just then Sue Yi turned, and Rui En's and her eyes locked. Sue Yi's usual calm expression changed instantly - from calm to betrayed. \"Why are you letting her control you?\" Sue Yi asked quietly. Sue Yi's words struck Rui En in the face as shame crashed over her. \"What was I doing?\" Rui En dropped the bin with a thud, tears burning in her eyes. \"I'm so sorry, Sue Yi,\" Rui En whispered. But Sue Yi turned away, devastated. Suddenly, a shriek cut through the market. Eileen had slipped and fallen on the wet floor, crashing right into the bin Rui En had just dropped. Slime and scraps exploded across Eileen's white shirt. Her phone, still streaming, captured the humiliating moment as laughter erupted from the crowd. Eileen's cheeks crimson red as she scrambled to her feet, desperately trying to wipe the mess from her clothes. Shock flickered across Sue Yi's face. Then as Rui En and Sue Yi looked at each other, Sue Yi's expression softened and melted into laughter. Rui En felt the tension in her chest ease; she realised how close she had come to losing the one person who truly cared about her. As Rui En knelt to clean the mess, she found herself staring at a sheep's eyeball - round, glossy, unblinking. Rui En picked it up with trembling fingers, a strange calm settling over her. \"Hey, Rui En,\" Sue Yi called softly. Rui En looked up to see her lifting her phone, her eyes shining with warmth despite everything. \"Maybe it's time we come clean. Show everyone at school what life in the wet market is really like. The real us.\" \"Smile,\" Sue Yi said. Rui En forced a shaky grin, a swirl of embarrassment and relief surging inside her. Yet beneath it all, something inside her had shifted. Later that evening, Sue Yi posted the photo with the caption: EYE bring out the best in her! For the first time, Rui En felt the 